1
00:00:06,950 --> 00:00:08,035
Enjoy!

2
00:00:11,369 --> 00:00:12,414
BFF!

3
00:00:12,951 --> 00:00:13,890
- BFF.
- BFF.

4
00:00:13,915 --> 00:00:14,965
How are you?

5
00:00:14,990 --> 00:00:16,091
I’m okay, BFF.

6
00:00:16,116 --> 00:00:17,423
No, I just wanted to ask something.

7
00:00:17,448 --> 00:00:18,273
Have a seat.

8
00:00:18,298 --> 00:00:21,658
Are you making bibingka
again this year like last time?

9
00:00:22,215 --> 00:00:23,438
Of course!

10
00:00:23,463 --> 00:00:25,183
How about you? What’s
your Christmas treat this year?

11
00:00:25,208 --> 00:00:26,941
I was actually hoping for the same thing…

12
00:00:26,966 --> 00:00:28,286
- What?
- Bibingka.

13
00:00:28,539 --> 00:00:29,506
- Bibingka?
- Mmm!

14
00:00:29,531 --> 00:00:32,498
Well, we’ll see, since you’re
selling them anyway, right?

15
00:00:32,523 --> 00:00:32,885
Yeah.

16
00:00:32,910 --> 00:00:33,919
Bibingka.

17
00:00:33,993 --> 00:00:35,100
Why do you sound mad?

18
00:00:35,125 --> 00:00:36,513
Are you in a bad mood?

19
00:00:37,025 --> 00:00:39,557
- Let’s cheer you up!
- It’s spilling over the edges!

20
00:00:39,582 --> 00:00:41,520
- Hello!
- Oh! Hello!

21
00:00:41,545 --> 00:00:42,798
Good day!

22
00:00:43,870 --> 00:00:45,783
Hello! Can I ask something?

23
00:00:45,808 --> 00:00:46,701
- Oh, sure!
- Yes!

24
00:00:46,739 --> 00:00:49,438
Is this Barangay Singko?

25
00:00:49,629 --> 00:00:51,174
Yes, this is Barangay Singko.

26
00:00:51,199 --> 00:00:53,386
I just wanted to know if…

27
00:00:53,519 --> 00:00:54,665
Wait…

28
00:00:55,793 --> 00:00:57,993
Don’t just start talking.

29
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:01,833
I know you!

30
00:01:01,948 --> 00:01:02,820
Huh?

31
00:01:03,139 --> 00:01:04,164
Huh?

32
00:01:04,531 --> 00:01:06,085
I’ve seen you before!

33
00:01:06,110 --> 00:01:07,626
I think I know her too.

34
00:01:07,651 --> 00:01:08,465
Eva.

35
00:01:08,490 --> 00:01:13,935
Oh! I own the… the lantern
shop in the next barangay.

36
00:01:14,164 --> 00:01:19,139
What’s it called again…? My shop’s
name is Pa-Star for All Seasons.

37
00:01:19,170 --> 00:01:22,124
- I knew it!
- Wow! So fabulous!

38
00:01:22,149 --> 00:01:23,715
She does that thing, right?

39
00:01:23,740 --> 00:01:30,161
That thing! Because she does this,
right?! That’s her! She does this thing!

40
00:01:30,186 --> 00:01:31,040
One more time!

41
00:01:31,065 --> 00:01:31,828
Is that really her?!

42
00:01:31,853 --> 00:01:32,428
No.

43
00:01:32,453 --> 00:01:33,925
The one where you lift you like this!

44
00:01:33,950 --> 00:01:35,202
- Can you still do that?
- No.

45
00:01:36,908 --> 00:01:38,281
It stings now!

46
00:01:38,320 --> 00:01:40,065
I just need a favor.

47
00:01:40,090 --> 00:01:43,498
I’m looking for a party I want to go to.

48
00:01:43,651 --> 00:01:44,674
Tso K!

49
00:01:44,699 --> 00:01:47,400
- Oh, what now? What now?
- What happened? Come on, tell us!

50
00:01:47,425 --> 00:01:49,073
You’re tired again! You
always come in tired!

51
00:01:49,098 --> 00:01:51,342
Chairman is inviting you guys.

52
00:01:51,405 --> 00:01:55,492
There’s a party, and
both of you are invited.

53
00:01:55,582 --> 00:01:59,049
Oh, maybe that’s the party
Miss Eva was talking about.

54
00:01:59,203 --> 00:02:02,610
That’s exactly the party
I’m looking for! Where is it?

55
00:02:02,635 --> 00:02:05,640
This is the senior citizens’ party.

56
00:02:05,665 --> 00:02:07,866
You don’t belong there;
you look way too young!

57
00:02:10,281 --> 00:02:12,401
A senior citizens’ party?

58
00:02:12,462 --> 00:02:14,862
You really shouldn’t
go there. It’s not for you.

59
00:02:14,893 --> 00:02:18,260
But if you just want to know
where it is, I can tell you.

60
00:03:18,505 --> 00:03:22,845
Then, sprinkle lots of coconut on top.

61
00:03:23,914 --> 00:03:28,873
Don’t be stingy because
that’s what our customers love.

62
00:03:29,150 --> 00:03:30,923
This looks like too much.

63
00:03:31,047 --> 00:03:32,687
Will we be able to finish all of it?

64
00:03:32,712 --> 00:03:34,218
We’re selling it, remember?

65
00:03:34,583 --> 00:03:37,515
Atasha, trust me,
during Christmas, this all

66
00:03:37,539 --> 00:03:40,471
sells out. People are
waiting outside for it.

67
00:03:41,116 --> 00:03:43,369
None of it will go to waste.

68
00:03:43,394 --> 00:03:47,908
It’s almost a tradition for the
people of Barangay Singko

69
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:52,365
to have Lola Maxi’s special
bibingka every Christmas.

70
00:03:52,571 --> 00:03:54,147
Really!

71
00:03:54,714 --> 00:04:00,916
You know, your Lolo Roman
really loved that bibingka…

72
00:04:00,941 --> 00:04:02,368
Lo–Lola Maxi,

73
00:04:03,418 --> 00:04:06,576
Okay, okay. Alright?

74
00:04:07,032 --> 00:04:08,899
Yes, your bibingka is delicious.

75
00:04:09,330 --> 00:04:10,890
Grandpa Roman loved it.

76
00:04:11,340 --> 00:04:12,567
Everything you make.

77
00:04:14,884 --> 00:04:16,644
He really loved it, huh?

78
00:04:16,669 --> 00:04:17,903
Your bibingka is really good!

79
00:04:19,476 --> 00:04:24,412
Guys, we were thinking we should bring
back the Christmas spirit in the barangay.

80
00:04:25,157 --> 00:04:28,704
Like Lola Maxi’s bibingka… Monito Monita!

81
00:04:31,933 --> 00:04:32,799
That’s a great idea!

82
00:04:32,885 --> 00:04:34,532
You know what, I’ll handle the draw!

83
00:04:34,709 --> 00:04:35,763
Go for it!

84
00:04:41,538 --> 00:04:42,998
Just relax and eat!

85
00:04:44,905 --> 00:04:46,985
We still have a lot to cook, Lola Maxi.

86
00:04:47,807 --> 00:04:50,114
Oh, not yet?

87
00:04:51,755 --> 00:04:53,622
What are you guys doing?

88
00:04:54,164 --> 00:04:59,297
Oh, Lola Maxi, we’re setting
up the Bibingka Station—

89
00:04:59,343 --> 00:05:00,968
BibingKarl!

90
00:05:02,688 --> 00:05:03,781
Yeah!

91
00:05:03,806 --> 00:05:07,669
But why are you setting up
here when you know it’s tradition

92
00:05:07,694 --> 00:05:11,492
that every Christmas, it’s
Lola Maxi who sells bibingka?

93
00:05:11,517 --> 00:05:12,268
Yeah, that’s right!

94
00:05:12,293 --> 00:05:15,112
Yeah, Iskineport, but
no one ever said you’re

95
00:05:15,137 --> 00:05:18,440
the only ones who can
sell bibingka here, right?

96
00:05:19,914 --> 00:05:23,507
So what, now you’re competing with us?

97
00:05:23,574 --> 00:05:24,068
Exactly.

98
00:05:24,277 --> 00:05:27,744
Well, kind of, but nothing personal.

99
00:05:27,959 --> 00:05:29,652
May the best bibingka win!

100
00:05:35,594 --> 00:05:36,694
Hey!

101
00:05:37,199 --> 00:05:38,545
Bibingka!

102
00:05:39,023 --> 00:05:41,036
Perfect timing—I’m craving bibingka!

103
00:05:41,061 --> 00:05:45,107
- Come here, then! Come, come!
- Come here, Boss Beauty!

104
00:05:45,204 --> 00:05:46,471
Our bibingka is delicious.

105
00:05:46,496 --> 00:05:48,148
You know it’s tried and tested.

106
00:05:48,174 --> 00:05:52,559
And if you buy
somewhere else, well… let’s

107
00:05:52,583 --> 00:05:57,612
just say your love life
might not be so lucky.

108
00:05:57,741 --> 00:05:59,434
- Boss Beauty!
- What?

109
00:05:59,820 --> 00:06:01,114
Buy from us!

110
00:06:01,300 --> 00:06:02,326
For a change!

111
00:06:02,385 --> 00:06:03,938
Do you always want
the same old thing?

112
00:06:04,783 --> 00:06:08,756
Choose! My bibingka, or do
you want me to punch you?

113
00:06:08,898 --> 00:06:09,452
What?

114
00:06:09,477 --> 00:06:12,757
Whoa, your sales pitch
sounds like a threat!

115
00:06:12,798 --> 00:06:20,425
Come here, Boss Beauty,
buy from Lola Bibingka!

116
00:06:20,450 --> 00:06:21,910
BibingKarl!

117
00:06:22,296 --> 00:06:23,962
BibingKarl!

118
00:06:24,201 --> 00:06:26,021
BibingKarl!

119
00:06:26,046 --> 00:06:28,674
No, this one’s tried and tested!

120
00:06:28,699 --> 00:06:30,007
Okay, close your eyes!

121
00:06:31,672 --> 00:06:32,789
I’ll go first.

122
00:06:32,814 --> 00:06:34,954
Hey, don’t fight over
it, everyone gets one!

123
00:06:36,054 --> 00:06:37,167
Go, pick!

124
00:06:37,192 --> 00:06:38,211
- There!
- Pick, pick!

125
00:06:40,199 --> 00:06:43,127
Oh, come on, this again?!

126
00:06:43,336 --> 00:06:47,047
Hey, whatever you got, keep it
to yourself, okay? It’s a secret!

127
00:06:47,642 --> 00:06:49,622
I’m not saying I picked you!

128
00:06:50,234 --> 00:06:52,427
You know, you could be cute,
but you’re kind of slow, huh?

129
00:06:52,855 --> 00:06:55,869
Wait, how is that possible?
I picked Osang too!

130
00:06:58,041 --> 00:06:59,001
Osang!

131
00:07:01,206 --> 00:07:04,733
Me too! Osang, you greedy thing!

132
00:07:05,374 --> 00:07:06,728
Don’t trick me!

133
00:07:07,326 --> 00:07:12,838
Fine, fine, I’ll do it!
Give it to me, I’ll write it!

134
00:07:13,374 --> 00:07:13,981
Seriously?!

135
00:07:14,013 --> 00:07:15,305
You haven’t changed,
Osang, since high school!

136
00:07:21,076 --> 00:07:21,867
Someone took the bait!

137
00:07:22,258 --> 00:07:28,350
We wish you a Merry Christmas, we wish you
a Merry Christmas, and a Happy New Year!

138
00:07:28,470 --> 00:07:29,563
Merry Christmas!

139
00:07:29,593 --> 00:07:32,200
Oh, sorry, not yet. No earnings yet.

140
00:07:32,679 --> 00:07:33,661
That’s okay…

141
00:07:34,239 --> 00:07:35,432
…I have a QR code!

142
00:07:35,611 --> 00:07:38,558
Wow, this kid is smart!

143
00:07:38,583 --> 00:07:39,567
Hey, kid!

144
00:07:39,855 --> 00:07:41,029
Hey, kid!

145
00:07:41,615 --> 00:07:42,055
Come here.

146
00:07:42,080 --> 00:07:43,132
- Why?
- What’s your name?

147
00:07:43,157 --> 00:07:44,114
Noel.

148
00:07:44,139 --> 00:07:47,258
Noel? Are you caroling?

149
00:07:47,286 --> 00:07:49,799
I have five pesos for you,
just for the spirit of giving!

150
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:53,460
Thank you!

151
00:07:54,273 --> 00:07:58,112
I hope your shop earns more
than the one across the street!

152
00:07:58,137 --> 00:08:00,794
- Hey!
- Oh wow, thanks!

153
00:08:00,819 --> 00:08:02,909
Come here! How much is that?

154
00:08:02,955 --> 00:08:03,729
Five.

155
00:08:03,754 --> 00:08:07,234
Oh, give him ten! That’s
only five? Give him ten!

156
00:08:07,259 --> 00:08:11,594
Noel, kid, Merry Christmas…

157
00:08:11,619 --> 00:08:17,048
- …I’ll give you twenty!
- Whoa, big spender!

158
00:08:17,079 --> 00:08:18,781
Hey, kid!

159
00:08:18,829 --> 00:08:19,155
Yes?

160
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:20,148
Don’t be too happy!

161
00:08:20,270 --> 00:08:21,370
- Why not?
- How much was that?

162
00:08:21,395 --> 00:08:22,582
Twenty.

163
00:08:22,607 --> 00:08:24,061
You’ll get fifty from me.

164
00:08:24,086 --> 00:08:27,118
- Whoa, whoa!
- Give him fifty!

165
00:08:27,143 --> 00:08:30,256
- Give him a hundred, Iskineport!
- Here, Lola, a hundred.

166
00:08:30,281 --> 00:08:32,227
Tso K, she said a hundred!

167
00:08:33,050 --> 00:08:35,753
Wow! A hundred!

168
00:08:35,778 --> 00:08:37,554
A hundred!

169
00:08:37,620 --> 00:08:38,914
Thank you!

170
00:08:38,939 --> 00:08:43,357
Yes, we’re winning!
We’re the lucky ones!

171
00:08:43,453 --> 00:08:47,680
Wait a minute—why did
you give him a hundred?!

172
00:08:48,535 --> 00:08:51,155
Lola Maxi, Tso K,

173
00:08:51,607 --> 00:08:55,374
don’t you realize you
got tricked by that kid?

174
00:08:55,399 --> 00:08:58,198
He took all your money!

175
00:09:04,948 --> 00:09:09,098
Okay, guys! Here comes
our first Kris Kringle!

176
00:09:11,019 --> 00:09:13,493
First category: something soft!

177
00:09:13,518 --> 00:09:16,605
Okay! I'll go first!

178
00:09:16,630 --> 00:09:17,684
Alright, alright!

179
00:09:17,709 --> 00:09:19,201
What could this be?

180
00:09:19,856 --> 00:09:22,150
Wow! A shirt!

181
00:09:22,176 --> 00:09:24,549
- It looks so nice!
- It looks great!

182
00:09:24,574 --> 00:09:25,993
It really suits you!

183
00:09:26,459 --> 00:09:29,052
Thank you, whoever you are!

184
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:32,086
Okay, okay, my turn!

185
00:09:32,166 --> 00:09:32,733
Go ahead.

186
00:09:33,106 --> 00:09:33,926
Oh!

187
00:09:35,116 --> 00:09:36,630
Wow! A pillow!

188
00:09:37,449 --> 00:09:38,976
And it even has my name on it!

189
00:09:39,256 --> 00:09:40,606
- Wow!
- Oh, that’s so nice.

190
00:09:40,631 --> 00:09:41,951
I wonder who it’s from?

191
00:09:42,239 --> 00:09:44,132
But thank you, thank you, mystery gifter!

192
00:09:44,157 --> 00:09:47,675
Wow, so far, so good!
I’m excited! Let’s see!

193
00:09:49,364 --> 00:09:49,964
Cotton balls?

194
00:09:51,985 --> 00:09:53,251
Were you saving money?

195
00:09:55,018 --> 00:09:55,991
Alright, my turn!

196
00:09:58,283 --> 00:10:01,756
Wow, Fluffy Mamon!
This is my favorite!

197
00:10:03,552 --> 00:10:05,472
That is my favorite!

198
00:10:08,011 --> 00:10:11,551
Oh, wait, now it’s my
turn! Let’s see mine.

199
00:10:12,404 --> 00:10:13,811
Let’s check this out.

200
00:10:17,701 --> 00:10:19,249
- Twenty?
- Twenty?

201
00:10:20,459 --> 00:10:21,953
Twenty pesos?!

202
00:10:22,405 --> 00:10:25,264
Here we go! Grand finale!

203
00:10:29,812 --> 00:10:30,995
Chewing gum?

204
00:10:32,715 --> 00:10:34,095
Do I have bad breath or what?

205
00:10:34,151 --> 00:10:35,253
Are you sure?

206
00:10:35,599 --> 00:10:36,546
You wish, Osang!

207
00:10:37,346 --> 00:10:38,472
Here we go, I’m opening it now.

208
00:10:42,146 --> 00:10:43,219
Thanks!

209
00:10:43,665 --> 00:10:46,632
Thank you, okay? Tell your sister, okay?

210
00:10:47,432 --> 00:10:48,303
Yes?

211
00:10:51,371 --> 00:10:52,615
Tell her.

212
00:10:53,021 --> 00:10:53,881
Tell her.

213
00:10:55,284 --> 00:10:56,458
- Mariposa!
- Yeah?

214
00:10:57,831 --> 00:10:58,897
Why?

215
00:10:59,165 --> 00:11:02,245
Tell that Tso K over there

216
00:11:03,749 --> 00:11:10,115
that he’s no longer invited to Kuya
Aga and his family’s Noche Buena!

217
00:11:16,819 --> 00:11:21,007
Hey, Iskineport, tell
your boss that my boss says,

218
00:11:21,031 --> 00:11:25,291
good thing he’s
not invited anymore.

219
00:11:25,603 --> 00:11:31,724
At least he doesn’t have to pretend
that his bland spaghetti is delicious!

220
00:11:32,991 --> 00:11:34,012
Whoa…

221
00:11:34,171 --> 00:11:35,538
Come here, come here!

222
00:11:35,706 --> 00:11:36,879
But honestly, it is a little bland.

223
00:11:42,387 --> 00:11:44,353
Lola Maxi, I’m getting dragged into this!

224
00:11:45,549 --> 00:11:54,363
Tell that Tso K that the only
thing bland here is his love life!

225
00:11:54,401 --> 00:11:57,317
Oh! That was harsh! That was brutal!

226
00:11:58,017 --> 00:11:59,050
That one really stings!

227
00:12:03,461 --> 00:12:11,530
Tell Lola Maxi, wow, says the
old lady who hasn’t had *** in ages!

228
00:12:14,812 --> 00:12:15,872
Oh my!

229
00:12:16,754 --> 00:12:20,181
That’s completely dried up then!
Completely dried up!

230
00:12:20,810 --> 00:12:23,464
Wait a minute, Lola Maxi,
am I getting paid for this?!

231
00:12:23,640 --> 00:12:25,560
Why don’t you just talk
to Tso K yourselves?!

232
00:12:25,585 --> 00:12:27,380
- Yeah, they should just…
- Fine, fine, fine!

233
00:12:27,808 --> 00:12:30,542
You know what, Karl,
you’re making this personal!

234
00:12:30,663 --> 00:12:31,916
- Me?!
- Yes!

235
00:12:31,941 --> 00:12:34,180
- No way!
- If you want, let’s settle this.

236
00:12:34,205 --> 00:12:35,747
- Go ahead.
- Let’s talk!

237
00:12:35,772 --> 00:12:38,008
- Alright.
- Fist to fist.

238
00:12:39,029 --> 00:12:41,253
- Oh no!
- Lola Maxi!

239
00:12:41,753 --> 00:12:44,560
- Let’s talk, Lola Maxi!
- No, no way!

240
00:12:44,591 --> 00:12:48,276
- I’m not making this personal!
- Hold on, hold on! Lola, Tsong!

241
00:12:48,301 --> 00:12:48,914
Yes?

242
00:12:48,939 --> 00:12:51,573
Don’t fight, it’s Christmas!

243
00:12:51,670 --> 00:12:54,697
There, listen to the kid.

244
00:12:54,915 --> 00:12:58,991
To settle this, why don’t
I just taste both of your

245
00:12:59,015 --> 00:13:03,091
bibingkas, so we can see
whose is actually better?

246
00:13:06,981 --> 00:13:09,821
Alright, taste mine.

247
00:13:09,846 --> 00:13:18,214
Hey, kid, try my new bibingka and see
if it’s better than Lola Maxi’s old one.

248
00:13:18,239 --> 00:13:20,677
Come here.

249
00:13:20,727 --> 00:13:23,927
This one was made with joy, by someone
who wasn’t robbed of their love life.

250
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:26,641
That was painful!

251
00:13:28,994 --> 00:13:30,003
Alright, kid!

252
00:13:32,388 --> 00:13:35,249
Here, new versus old, young versus old.

253
00:13:35,280 --> 00:13:37,289
I think… Lola’s bibingka!

254
00:13:37,647 --> 00:13:38,644
Yes!

255
00:13:40,304 --> 00:13:42,077
Wait, wait, wait, wait.
Let me taste it again.

256
00:13:42,102 --> 00:13:43,229
Oh, he’s taking another bite.

257
00:13:45,240 --> 00:13:46,853
Oh, wait, I think I like Tso K’s better!

258
00:13:46,878 --> 00:13:49,248
Woooh! Go, Tso K!

259
00:13:50,463 --> 00:13:51,243
Hold on…

260
00:13:51,277 --> 00:13:52,224
Huh?

261
00:13:52,249 --> 00:13:53,216
Let me try again.

262
00:13:55,886 --> 00:13:59,099
Here! I’ll give you the whole thing!

263
00:14:00,634 --> 00:14:02,108
Wait, I’m having trouble deciding.

264
00:14:02,133 --> 00:14:03,179
Can I have a drink?

265
00:14:03,798 --> 00:14:06,095
Now he wants a drink?!

266
00:14:06,284 --> 00:14:07,031
It’s okay!

267
00:14:07,056 --> 00:14:09,852
Oh, oh, give him another
one, give him another one!

268
00:14:10,505 --> 00:14:12,978
Here, take it! Take everything!

269
00:14:15,397 --> 00:14:16,749
Give him a plate too!

270
00:14:17,963 --> 00:14:21,756
Didn’t he say multiple
times that mine was better?!

271
00:14:21,781 --> 00:14:27,368
Hold on! Hold on! Hold
on! Tso K, Lola Maxi…

272
00:14:27,393 --> 00:14:28,109
Yes?

273
00:14:28,134 --> 00:14:29,436
Didn’t you guys notice?

274
00:14:30,460 --> 00:14:32,013
That kid was just playing you!

275
00:14:32,781 --> 00:14:35,814
You fed him, then gave him five takeouts!

276
00:14:36,064 --> 00:14:38,171
My goodness! That kid tricked you!

277
00:14:38,524 --> 00:14:43,427
Aga, please, can you just end
your friendship with Karl already?

278
00:14:43,452 --> 00:14:47,004
Imagine, trying to compete
with me in business?

279
00:14:48,729 --> 00:14:54,235
Lola Maxi, I don’t control BFF’s life.

280
00:14:54,285 --> 00:14:56,959
Just let him be. His mind
is always all over the place.

281
00:14:57,245 --> 00:15:01,968
And honestly, there’s nothing wrong with
a little healthy competition, Lola Maxi.

282
00:15:02,035 --> 00:15:03,004
Healthy?!

283
00:15:03,029 --> 00:15:06,576
How is that healthy when my
blood pressure is going up?!

284
00:15:06,789 --> 00:15:07,856
Healthy, my foot!

285
00:15:07,881 --> 00:15:09,172
Who did you pick for Kris Kringle?

286
00:15:09,838 --> 00:15:12,998
I’m not telling, but I
picked a special one.

287
00:15:13,178 --> 00:15:15,171
So, you picked me?

288
00:15:15,666 --> 00:15:17,692
That’s cheap! You gave
me cotton balls as a gift?!

289
00:15:17,717 --> 00:15:19,901
Hey, no way! I didn’t pick you!

290
00:15:20,345 --> 00:15:20,991
Huh?!

291
00:15:21,313 --> 00:15:26,691
But you know, that’s so sweet of you,
because I know you gave this to me.

292
00:15:26,882 --> 00:15:28,569
Hey, that’s not from me!

293
00:15:28,594 --> 00:15:29,113
Maybe it’s from Anne.

294
00:15:29,188 --> 00:15:32,668
Nope. I think Francis picked her.

295
00:15:33,420 --> 00:15:34,640
Francis? Aww…

296
00:15:35,076 --> 00:15:36,869
Did you see that mamon earlier?

297
00:15:36,894 --> 00:15:41,732
- Are you jealous of Francis?
- Hey, no! No way! No, no, no!

298
00:15:42,645 --> 00:15:44,878
Busted! He loves me…

299
00:15:44,903 --> 00:15:47,270
Oh, I think you’re jealous!

300
00:15:48,085 --> 00:15:50,490
I know that look
when you’re jealous!

301
00:15:56,685 --> 00:15:59,173
Okay, guys, round two
of the exchange gifts!

302
00:15:59,261 --> 00:16:01,888
The category is something hard!

303
00:16:02,059 --> 00:16:03,638
I'll go first, okay? Me first.

304
00:16:05,103 --> 00:16:08,923
Wow! My monito
made up for it, look!

305
00:16:09,034 --> 00:16:10,074
Perfume!

306
00:16:10,099 --> 00:16:11,894
- Wow!
- That’s awesome!

307
00:16:14,545 --> 00:16:15,489
Huh?

308
00:16:16,448 --> 00:16:17,458
It’s empty!

309
00:16:18,985 --> 00:16:20,391
So it’s just the bottle?

310
00:16:24,250 --> 00:16:27,587
Even if it’s just a
bottle, Tash, it’s still

311
00:16:27,611 --> 00:16:30,948
cheaper than the twenty
pesos I got in coins!

312
00:16:33,179 --> 00:16:34,119
At least you can use it.

313
00:16:34,896 --> 00:16:36,282
Maybe you deserved that, right?

314
00:16:37,244 --> 00:16:39,431
You deserved that! You
deserved that, Osang!

315
00:16:39,739 --> 00:16:42,052
But wasn’t the rule “something hard”?

316
00:16:42,718 --> 00:16:44,458
Why does this feel like
something heavy too?

317
00:16:46,977 --> 00:16:47,897
That still counts!

318
00:16:47,922 --> 00:16:48,656
Oh!

319
00:16:48,681 --> 00:16:49,722
Mmm, a rock!

320
00:16:50,447 --> 00:16:53,151
Whoever gave this, I
swear I’ll throw it back at you!

321
00:16:53,759 --> 00:16:56,119
Okay, okay, my turn!

322
00:16:57,709 --> 00:16:59,176
A hard box!

323
00:16:59,442 --> 00:17:00,727
There’s something inside!

324
00:17:00,752 --> 00:17:02,245
Oh, chocolate!

325
00:17:02,270 --> 00:17:04,654
Hey, share some!

326
00:17:04,679 --> 00:17:06,058
Let’s each have one!

327
00:17:06,090 --> 00:17:08,230
So sweet of my gifter!

328
00:17:08,255 --> 00:17:10,030
Me next, me next, me next!

329
00:17:12,455 --> 00:17:14,255
Oh, mine is so sweet too!

330
00:17:14,853 --> 00:17:16,713
A personalized tumbler!

331
00:17:16,738 --> 00:17:19,247
- Wow!
- That’s awesome!

332
00:17:19,272 --> 00:17:20,927
They knew I lost my old tumbler!

333
00:17:21,788 --> 00:17:24,475
Thanks, Tash! I can
use this for basketball!

334
00:17:24,500 --> 00:17:26,185
Hey, that wasn’t me! You’re so stubborn!

335
00:17:26,352 --> 00:17:26,939
Huh?

336
00:17:27,351 --> 00:17:28,205
Oh, my turn!

337
00:17:32,292 --> 00:17:34,096
- Perfect, a ball!
- Oh, a basketball!

338
00:17:34,838 --> 00:17:36,331
Anyone up to play?
- Fancy!

339
00:17:36,606 --> 00:17:37,709
- Me, me, me!
- Game!

340
00:17:37,793 --> 00:17:38,532
- Let’s play!
- Catch this, okay?

341
00:17:38,557 --> 00:17:39,457
Don’t hit me, okay?

342
00:17:40,782 --> 00:17:43,182
If you hit me, I’m throwing
it right back at you.

343
00:17:44,070 --> 00:17:44,656
Let me join!

344
00:17:44,681 --> 00:17:45,276
Nice one!

345
00:17:45,301 --> 00:17:46,176
Let me in!

346
00:17:46,305 --> 00:17:47,298
Okay, Andres is in.

347
00:17:47,509 --> 00:17:48,236
Pass it.

348
00:17:48,261 --> 00:17:49,238
Catch it, okay?

349
00:17:51,425 --> 00:17:53,645
Oh, okay. Francis, catch this!

350
00:17:53,725 --> 00:17:54,443
Game!

351
00:17:54,468 --> 00:17:55,188
Oh!

352
00:17:55,213 --> 00:17:55,746
Oh!

353
00:17:55,771 --> 00:17:56,706
Sorry!

354
00:17:56,731 --> 00:17:58,064
Hey, are you okay?

355
00:17:58,493 --> 00:17:59,526
Does it hurt?

356
00:18:04,285 --> 00:18:05,418
Sorry, sorry!

357
00:18:05,443 --> 00:18:06,309
Blow on it, blow on it.

358
00:18:07,919 --> 00:18:09,646
What is this, magic?
Or does it really hurt?

359
00:18:10,370 --> 00:18:11,410
Does it hurt?

360
00:18:24,532 --> 00:18:25,500
Oh, Noel!

361
00:18:26,487 --> 00:18:27,664
- What are you doing here?
- Hi, Tsong!

362
00:18:27,856 --> 00:18:30,198
Ate Mariposa asked
me to stay here for a bit

363
00:18:30,223 --> 00:18:32,566
while she picked up
something from your spa.

364
00:18:33,266 --> 00:18:33,957
Ah.

365
00:18:34,266 --> 00:18:34,648
Oh!

366
00:18:35,549 --> 00:18:38,180
Hey, where’s Iskineport?

367
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:40,243
Oh, Lola, he just went to the restroom.

368
00:18:41,201 --> 00:18:44,334
Uh, Lola, I have to go now.
I still have to go caroling.

369
00:18:44,496 --> 00:18:45,436
- Oh, alright.
- Alright, take care.

370
00:18:47,505 --> 00:18:48,504
Hey!

371
00:18:48,529 --> 00:18:51,385
What’s this?! Why is it empty?!

372
00:18:51,818 --> 00:18:52,799
Oh!

373
00:18:53,606 --> 00:18:55,590
Mine too! The stuff inside is gone!

374
00:18:55,730 --> 00:18:56,390
What?!

375
00:18:56,793 --> 00:19:01,950
I knew it! I knew that kid
was up to something again!

376
00:19:02,402 --> 00:19:04,905
That kid is unbelievable!

377
00:19:05,420 --> 00:19:08,172
Turns out he’s a little thief!

378
00:19:09,007 --> 00:19:12,255
I knew it! I knew it!

379
00:19:13,276 --> 00:19:16,379
You know, when they’re young,
you have to cut their horns early!

380
00:19:16,763 --> 00:19:17,666
You know what we should do?

381
00:19:17,842 --> 00:19:21,794
We should find him and
punish him until he collapses!

382
00:19:21,819 --> 00:19:24,182
Whoa, that’s too much!
You’d punish him right away?!

383
00:19:24,207 --> 00:19:24,625
Exactly!

384
00:19:24,696 --> 00:19:27,666
Hey, hey, hold on.
Hold on. No need for that.

385
00:19:27,691 --> 00:19:31,300
A kid can be talked to or scolded.

386
00:19:31,325 --> 00:19:32,494
No need for punishment.

387
00:19:32,519 --> 00:19:35,127
Oh no, Lola Maxi! That won’t work!

388
00:19:35,319 --> 00:19:39,974
Fine, let’s do this instead—I’ll
scold him using my fists!

389
00:19:40,092 --> 00:19:42,237
Yeah, my fists! Like this!

390
00:19:42,262 --> 00:19:44,082
- Hey!
- That’s not okay!

391
00:19:44,107 --> 00:19:45,868
- That’s way too much!
- Come here!

392
00:19:45,917 --> 00:19:47,941
You’d resort to violence right away?!

393
00:19:47,965 --> 00:19:50,069
- Yeah, like this!
- That would hurt!

394
00:19:50,974 --> 00:19:52,981
- Come here, come here!
- You can’t just hit someone like that.

395
00:19:53,012 --> 00:19:54,543
- Come here, Karl.
- What is it, Lola Maxi?

396
00:19:54,568 --> 00:19:56,374
- Let’s call a ceasefire for now.
- Yes, Lola.

397
00:19:57,256 --> 00:19:59,007
We have a common enemy.

398
00:19:59,062 --> 00:19:59,910
Okay?

399
00:19:59,935 --> 00:20:00,987
Let’s find him.

400
00:20:01,012 --> 00:20:02,236
- There we go!
- Right?!

401
00:20:02,261 --> 00:20:04,353
Let’s find him!
Alright, let’s go.

402
00:20:10,645 --> 00:20:14,211
Hey, in fairness to
your gifter—first, a shirt.

403
00:20:14,549 --> 00:20:16,537
Then, chocolates.

404
00:20:16,971 --> 00:20:18,020
It’s like they’re courting you!

405
00:20:18,503 --> 00:20:21,279
Whoever they are, I got lucky with them.

406
00:20:21,833 --> 00:20:23,724
They know exactly what I like.

407
00:20:25,088 --> 00:20:27,063
What about you? Who did you pick?

408
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:30,749
That’s a secret! Someone special!

409
00:20:31,901 --> 00:20:33,088
Oh, Francis, huh?

410
00:20:33,843 --> 00:20:38,000
Andres said he knew you
made that mamon he got!

411
00:20:39,914 --> 00:20:40,932
Okay, fine.

412
00:20:42,322 --> 00:20:46,049
The mamon was from
me, but I didn’t pick Francis.

413
00:20:46,551 --> 00:20:50,115
You’ll just find out tomorrow
who we all picked. Right?

414
00:20:50,246 --> 00:20:51,543
- Huh?
- Right?

415
00:20:51,568 --> 00:20:54,551
How was it from you,
but you didn’t pick him?

416
00:20:55,086 --> 00:20:59,387
You know, you and Francis are so
confusing, that’s why Andres is jealous!

417
00:20:59,793 --> 00:21:00,684
He’s jealous?

418
00:21:00,709 --> 00:21:01,054
Huh?

419
00:21:01,155 --> 00:21:04,143
Mmm, I didn’t say
anything. Nope, not at all.

420
00:21:04,263 --> 00:21:05,002
Is that true?

421
00:21:05,033 --> 00:21:07,162
Wait, I’m just going to enjoy
this perfume! Bye, okay, see ya!

422
00:21:07,314 --> 00:21:09,217
Hey! That bottle is empty!

423
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:11,484
Tash!

424
00:21:12,195 --> 00:21:13,258
Where did she go?!

425
00:21:27,579 --> 00:21:28,585
Eat up…

426
00:21:37,161 --> 00:21:38,088
Karl!

427
00:21:40,131 --> 00:21:41,198
Hey!

428
00:21:41,903 --> 00:21:43,630
So this is where you’ve been hiding, huh?!

429
00:21:44,247 --> 00:21:45,816
I’m not hiding.

430
00:21:45,841 --> 00:21:47,538
- What do you mean you’re not hiding?!
- Oh no, Noel!

431
00:21:47,653 --> 00:21:48,326
Oh no, huh!

432
00:21:48,617 --> 00:21:50,926
Hey, give back what
you took from us!

433
00:21:51,060 --> 00:21:52,272
I didn’t take anything!

434
00:21:52,320 --> 00:21:53,563
What do you mean you
didn’t take anything?!

435
00:21:53,871 --> 00:21:55,683
Come on, Noel, stop lying!

436
00:21:56,220 --> 00:21:59,620
First, you already tricked us.

437
00:21:59,978 --> 00:22:01,826
Second, you fooled
us with the bibingka.

438
00:22:02,027 --> 00:22:05,784
So it’s not far-fetched to
think you took our money!

439
00:22:05,809 --> 00:22:06,706
That’s right!

440
00:22:08,769 --> 00:22:12,413
Noel, son, is it true that you stole?

441
00:22:12,971 --> 00:22:14,838
No, Mom, I swear!

442
00:22:15,206 --> 00:22:15,882
Oh no!

443
00:22:15,907 --> 00:22:18,477
We may be poor, but I would never do that.

444
00:22:18,787 --> 00:22:19,810
There they are, Mariposa!

445
00:22:19,835 --> 00:22:22,944
That’s them talking
over there! I told you!

446
00:22:22,984 --> 00:22:23,863
Here!

447
00:22:23,888 --> 00:22:25,300
What Noel is saying is true!

448
00:22:25,325 --> 00:22:30,460
We heard you from far away! He
didn’t take the money, Lola Maxi!

449
00:22:30,727 --> 00:22:31,708
Then who did?!

450
00:22:31,733 --> 00:22:35,788
You lent it to Ate Cha for the
Noche Buena preparations.

451
00:22:36,237 --> 00:22:39,796
And besides, Tso K, our
money was already gone, right?

452
00:22:39,835 --> 00:22:44,823
Remember, we used it to buy
ingredients for the bibingka?

453
00:22:44,848 --> 00:22:46,462
- That’s what that was?
- Yes!

454
00:22:48,451 --> 00:22:50,994
Good thing we followed you
here because we overheard you!

455
00:22:51,021 --> 00:22:53,593
Boss Beauty said you were
planning to beat up Noel

456
00:22:53,617 --> 00:22:56,190
so bad that only his eyes
would be left unbruised.

457
00:22:56,215 --> 00:22:58,425
Hey! That’s not—That’s not true!

458
00:22:58,450 --> 00:22:59,407
That’s what you said!

459
00:22:59,432 --> 00:23:00,298
No, it’s not!

460
00:23:00,323 --> 00:23:03,536
No, the reason we came
here is that I wanted to see Noel

461
00:23:03,561 --> 00:23:07,355
and tell him that
he’s actually a good kid.

462
00:23:07,380 --> 00:23:09,427
That’s true, Mom!

463
00:23:09,498 --> 00:23:11,080
He really is a good kid.

464
00:23:11,135 --> 00:23:19,074
In fact, we’re here because we
wanted to give Noel unlimited bibingka.

465
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:20,672
Right, Karl?

466
00:23:20,697 --> 00:23:21,252
Yes!

467
00:23:22,362 --> 00:23:23,628
- Really?
- Of course!

468
00:23:24,247 --> 00:23:26,253
Son, son, help me up.

469
00:23:32,074 --> 00:23:34,773
Oh, his mom is sick, poor thing.

470
00:23:35,608 --> 00:23:39,740
I never taught my son to be a bad person!

471
00:23:40,207 --> 00:23:42,328
And no one taught me to be one either!

472
00:23:43,252 --> 00:23:44,943
And now you want to hurt my son?!

473
00:23:44,968 --> 00:23:47,454
- No, no.
- I’ll beat you to it!

474
00:23:55,261 --> 00:23:57,134
Where are you all going?! Huh?!

475
00:23:57,159 --> 00:23:58,884
- Mom, stop!
- Come back here!

476
00:24:01,648 --> 00:24:03,466
Okay, guys, this is it!

477
00:24:03,491 --> 00:24:06,467
The final round
of exchange gifts!

478
00:24:07,764 --> 00:24:10,346
Category is something special.

479
00:24:10,371 --> 00:24:13,900
But this time, we reveal who
picked whom, okay?

480
00:24:14,010 --> 00:24:15,022
- Okay!
- Okay!

481
00:24:15,125 --> 00:24:15,688
Game!

482
00:24:16,448 --> 00:24:18,539
Something special!

483
00:24:20,655 --> 00:24:21,806
A picture frame?!

484
00:24:22,388 --> 00:24:23,825
And it’s dusty?

485
00:24:25,019 --> 00:24:28,116
Who gave me this so I
can at least say thanks?

486
00:24:30,363 --> 00:24:31,769
Osang?!

487
00:24:32,200 --> 00:24:33,473
Sorry, Tash…

488
00:24:34,109 --> 00:24:35,752
I really didn’t have any cash.

489
00:24:35,859 --> 00:24:37,114
But I made up for it!

490
00:24:37,302 --> 00:24:37,790
With what?

491
00:24:37,815 --> 00:24:41,482
Here! Put this in the frame—I had a
group picture of us printed with the parol!

492
00:24:42,757 --> 00:24:45,587
- Wow!
- That’s so sweet!

493
00:24:46,588 --> 00:24:49,309
At least it has sentimental value!

494
00:24:49,501 --> 00:24:50,265
Okay, your turn!

495
00:24:50,421 --> 00:24:52,869
What did you get?
Something special.

496
00:24:59,429 --> 00:25:01,653
Wow!

497
00:25:01,701 --> 00:25:03,877
Not cash anymore, but a check!

498
00:25:04,016 --> 00:25:06,883
And… oh! There’s a message on the back!

499
00:25:07,235 --> 00:25:11,515
"Dear Osang, I’m happy to
be your friend. Love, Pippa!"

500
00:25:11,648 --> 00:25:15,939
Aww, that’s so sweet! I’m actually
getting emotional! I’m touched!

501
00:25:15,963 --> 00:25:19,864
Let’s check how much it’s for… and…

502
00:25:20,994 --> 00:25:22,073
twenty pesos?

503
00:25:23,225 --> 00:25:24,243
You even wrote a check for that.

504
00:25:24,268 --> 00:25:27,025
You’re so extra! At least you got sixty
pesos. And me? What did I get? A rock?!

505
00:25:27,235 --> 00:25:28,054
Whatever!

506
00:25:28,433 --> 00:25:33,300
But I hope I can at least make it up
to whoever gifted me this! Hold on…

507
00:25:35,428 --> 00:25:36,641
A jewelry box?!

508
00:25:36,666 --> 00:25:37,810
There it is!

509
00:25:38,839 --> 00:25:42,118
Oh my god, whoever gave
me this, you know me so well.

510
00:25:46,038 --> 00:25:52,137
Prank! Sorry, sorry, that was
me! You know I’m a prankster.

511
00:25:52,403 --> 00:25:54,487
Tash, you are officially out of this game.

512
00:25:54,512 --> 00:25:55,637
You’re unbelievable!

513
00:25:55,662 --> 00:25:59,310
Okay, my turn! Enough
talking, I’m excited about this!

514
00:26:02,774 --> 00:26:05,937
Wow, a t-shirt! And it has a special print!

515
00:26:07,122 --> 00:26:10,742
"I love Francis. The most
handsome guy in Barangay Singko."

516
00:26:10,799 --> 00:26:13,854
- Wow!
- Wow!

517
00:26:14,925 --> 00:26:17,975
Wow, Anne, your
gift-giving is on another level.

518
00:26:18,210 --> 00:26:19,683
Not only is he handsome, but
you even put "I love you" on it?

519
00:26:20,885 --> 00:26:22,885
Huh? What are you talking about?!

520
00:26:23,285 --> 00:26:24,685
Don’t even try to deny it!

521
00:26:25,023 --> 00:26:26,490
You made the mamon, didn’t you?

522
00:26:27,248 --> 00:26:33,219
Yes, I gave him the mamon, but…
Francis, tell them, who did you pick?!

523
00:26:33,467 --> 00:26:34,503
Who did I pick?

524
00:26:34,762 --> 00:26:36,059
- Yeah!
- Myself!

525
00:26:36,920 --> 00:26:40,657
That actually worked out because
at least I got exactly what I wanted.

526
00:26:40,932 --> 00:26:43,490
I just had Anne make the mamon for me.

527
00:26:44,476 --> 00:26:48,862
Huh? So the basketball and
the shirt weren’t from Anne?

528
00:26:49,275 --> 00:26:50,166
Nope!

529
00:26:52,833 --> 00:26:54,736
Oh, okay. I’ll open mine now.

530
00:26:58,807 --> 00:27:00,323
Wow, a stuffed toy!

531
00:27:00,626 --> 00:27:02,765
It looks like… An-An!

532
00:27:02,796 --> 00:27:04,163
Our puppy! Right?!

533
00:27:05,467 --> 00:27:10,489
First, I gave you a pillow
so you could sleep soundly.

534
00:27:15,022 --> 00:27:18,482
Second, a tumbler because
I know you need one.

535
00:27:22,203 --> 00:27:26,330
And the last one, An-An,
because I know you miss him.

536
00:27:29,775 --> 00:27:33,381
I was the one who picked you.

537
00:27:33,956 --> 00:27:34,816
Merry Christmas!

538
00:27:35,378 --> 00:27:38,651
Thank you, thank you!

539
00:27:38,676 --> 00:27:39,396
Your turn!

540
00:27:39,459 --> 00:27:42,114
Alright, I’m the last one. ?

541
00:27:42,967 --> 00:27:44,122
What could this be

542
00:27:45,535 --> 00:27:47,784
Wow!

543
00:27:51,044 --> 00:27:52,818
Andres, was this you?!

544
00:27:53,522 --> 00:27:54,685
You drew me?!

545
00:27:56,926 --> 00:27:59,912
And the chocolates, and
even the outfit I’m wearing?!

546
00:28:00,274 --> 00:28:01,699
That looks perfect on you?

547
00:28:02,274 --> 00:28:03,141
Yeah, that was me.

548
00:28:03,166 --> 00:28:04,281
Merry Christmas!

549
00:28:05,165 --> 00:28:06,365
That's so nice.

550
00:28:08,847 --> 00:28:10,266
Thank you, really!

551
00:28:13,802 --> 00:28:18,159
Anne, thanks so much for your gifts.

552
00:28:18,990 --> 00:28:20,188
I was really touched.

553
00:28:20,770 --> 00:28:23,685
Thanks for your gifts
too. I got butterflies!

554
00:28:25,197 --> 00:28:26,797
Ah, I’ll just take this.

555
00:28:42,985 --> 00:28:45,070
What do you mean by that, Anne?

556
00:28:48,492 --> 00:28:49,533
So we’re going official?

557
00:28:49,558 --> 00:28:50,531
We’re going official?

558
00:28:57,648 --> 00:29:01,169
You know, we can always
just sleep on this first, right?

559
00:29:01,762 --> 00:29:05,265
Yeah, yeah. That’s right.
So we can think about it.

560
00:29:06,298 --> 00:29:09,995
Let’s just… not tell anyone for now?

561
00:29:10,759 --> 00:29:16,365
Of course! But at least
we know it’s mutual, right?

562
00:29:17,620 --> 00:29:18,822
Mmm!

563
00:29:18,847 --> 00:29:21,671
Mutual understanding. MU!

564
00:29:22,627 --> 00:29:24,754
Okay, I’ll go ahead, Andres.

565
00:29:25,199 --> 00:29:26,274
MU.

566
00:29:26,860 --> 00:29:27,797
Bye!

567
00:29:29,585 --> 00:29:30,531
Bye!

568
00:29:55,764 --> 00:30:00,617
Oh my god! The An-an
ship is finally sailing!

569
00:30:12,108 --> 00:30:16,442
- Wow!
- Your salad is so good!

570
00:30:16,709 --> 00:30:18,497
Hey!

571
00:30:19,307 --> 00:30:22,523
- Ho, ho, ho!
- Oh wow, you even dressed up!

572
00:30:22,613 --> 00:30:27,716
Merry Christmas, and a happy new year!

573
00:30:30,438 --> 00:30:31,262
BFF!

574
00:30:34,831 --> 00:30:36,594
I’ll share this with everyone.

575
00:30:36,885 --> 00:30:39,322
- Oh!
- Oh!

576
00:30:39,680 --> 00:30:41,989
Are you two good now?

577
00:30:43,371 --> 00:30:44,244
Are you?

578
00:30:44,682 --> 00:30:45,828
Let’s see!

579
00:30:47,725 --> 00:30:48,974
What do you say, Lola Maxi?

580
00:30:49,204 --> 00:30:50,653
Hey, this is actually good!

581
00:30:55,004 --> 00:30:59,888
There you go! Come on, let’s eat!

582
00:31:01,014 --> 00:31:02,341
- BFF!
- Ah, yes?

583
00:31:02,431 --> 00:31:06,334
Sorry to interrupt, but
I also invited someone.

584
00:31:06,599 --> 00:31:10,576
Hope they can join us, if that’s okay?

585
00:31:10,608 --> 00:31:12,905
Of course! Look at all this food!

586
00:31:12,930 --> 00:31:14,642
There’s so much food! Go ahead!

587
00:31:14,925 --> 00:31:16,434
Ah, Noel! Noel!

588
00:31:18,057 --> 00:31:19,033
Come in!

589
00:31:20,635 --> 00:31:23,078
Hello, dig in! Welcome!

590
00:31:23,103 --> 00:31:26,084
Thank you so much for inviting us!

591
00:31:26,109 --> 00:31:28,899
Mom, the food is amazing!

592
00:31:29,707 --> 00:31:31,362
I’m going to eat a lot!

593
00:31:31,387 --> 00:31:34,978
Oh, you better! Come on, let’s all eat!

594
00:31:56,881 --> 00:31:58,735
Merry Christmas, everyone!

595
00:31:59,390 --> 00:32:06,340
I’m so happy that my family and I
can spend this Christmas with you.

596
00:32:06,365 --> 00:32:10,704
And not just this Christmas, but every
Christmas. Thank you so, so much.

597
00:32:10,751 --> 00:32:13,400
- Of course, BFF!
- Oh, you’re here!

598
00:32:13,425 --> 00:32:17,127
I’m here. Well, you always say it, right?

599
00:32:17,752 --> 00:32:24,772
Through ups and downs,
Pers is first, Pers is the star!

600
00:32:31,210 --> 00:32:37,155
Wait, I also want to
thank the kids, because

601
00:32:37,181 --> 00:32:42,896
the inter-barangay gift
exchange was their idea!

602
00:32:44,368 --> 00:32:47,428
So, we’re all happy, and… what?

603
00:32:47,546 --> 00:32:50,265
Should I open this?! I’ll go first!

604
00:32:55,042 --> 00:32:56,866
Thanks, thanks!

605
00:32:56,932 --> 00:33:03,209
- That’s from me, Ate Cha!
- Oh, thanks, Mariposa! Thanks!

606
00:33:03,811 --> 00:33:04,874
Your turn!

607
00:33:08,454 --> 00:33:09,538
A mug too?!

608
00:33:09,727 --> 00:33:11,108
From me!

609
00:33:12,731 --> 00:33:14,961
What could this be?! A mug too?!

610
00:33:16,049 --> 00:33:18,570
Wait, let’s open it!

611
00:33:19,813 --> 00:33:21,328
A mug too?!

612
00:33:29,514 --> 00:33:31,818
Hold on! Merry—

613
00:33:31,843 --> 00:33:35,325
Christmas!

614
00:33:41,495 --> 00:33:42,150
What?!

615
00:33:42,175 --> 00:33:43,063
BFF.

616
00:33:43,088 --> 00:33:47,207
BFF, nothing, I was just
thinking. You look deep in thought.

617
00:33:47,237 --> 00:33:51,793
I was just thinking,
this past year was great.

618
00:33:52,101 --> 00:33:58,309
But happiness comes
from sadness too, right?

619
00:33:58,831 --> 00:33:59,501
Happiness?

620
00:33:59,526 --> 00:34:00,544
- Happiness.
- Happiness.

621
00:34:00,569 --> 00:34:01,593
I knew you were going there.

622
00:34:01,618 --> 00:34:02,514
Do you get what I mean?

623
00:34:02,539 --> 00:34:06,341
No, I just realized that in
everything we’ve been through, even

624
00:34:06,365 --> 00:34:10,105
our friendship, there were
fights. That’s just how life is.

625
00:34:10,225 --> 00:34:12,807
But in the end, it’s always happy.

626
00:34:12,845 --> 00:34:13,360
Happy.

627
00:34:13,435 --> 00:34:15,084
Right, happy.

628
00:34:15,270 --> 00:34:16,676
So stop overthinking.

629
00:34:16,701 --> 00:34:18,197
Hi, how are you?

630
00:34:18,222 --> 00:34:20,856
- Oh! Hello, Miss Eva!
- Miss Eva!

631
00:34:21,654 --> 00:34:24,285
How are you? Did you enjoy the party?

632
00:34:24,310 --> 00:34:27,771
Oh, I did! I had so much
fun, even though I wasn’t

633
00:34:27,795 --> 00:34:31,257
invited, they still welcomed
me! It was so much fun!

634
00:34:31,355 --> 00:34:32,716
- You know, Tso—
- Ouch!

635
00:34:33,181 --> 00:34:34,878
You totally fit in there!

636
00:34:34,903 --> 00:34:35,767
Where?

637
00:34:35,792 --> 00:34:37,810
At the party I crashed!

638
00:34:37,853 --> 00:34:39,973
That’s not for me! I
don’t like being uninvited!

639
00:34:39,998 --> 00:34:40,919
Miss Eva!

640
00:34:40,944 --> 00:34:42,055
Miss Eva!

641
00:34:42,633 --> 00:34:43,637
- What?!
- Wow!

642
00:34:43,669 --> 00:34:48,160
I just came from the party. You left
something behind—your raffle prize.

643
00:34:48,328 --> 00:34:49,096
Here!

644
00:34:49,121 --> 00:34:50,567
Come here, come here!

645
00:34:51,662 --> 00:34:53,553
What is this? Wait a sec.

646
00:34:53,578 --> 00:34:54,517
- Let’s open it.
- Huh?

647
00:34:54,542 --> 00:34:56,178
- Let’s open it!
- Let’s open it!

648
00:34:56,203 --> 00:34:58,133
Wait, hold on. Did I
really leave this there?

649
00:34:58,158 --> 00:34:58,945
Yes!

650
00:34:58,970 --> 00:35:00,619
Maybe this is what—

651
00:35:00,650 --> 00:35:02,797
- What is this?
- There, there. Hold on.

652
00:35:03,100 --> 00:35:04,185
What is this? Huh?

653
00:35:04,210 --> 00:35:06,026
- I don’t know either!
- This is for arthritis, huh?

654
00:35:06,051 --> 00:35:08,913
Wait, why is this all for knees?!

655
00:35:09,697 --> 00:35:10,594
This too—

656
00:35:10,619 --> 00:35:12,279
Why does this all seem
like old people stuff?!

657
00:35:12,304 --> 00:35:13,948
Oh wow, for arthritis!

658
00:35:13,973 --> 00:35:15,995
I told you, that’s not yours!

659
00:35:16,020 --> 00:35:17,294
What’s your name again?

660
00:35:17,319 --> 00:35:19,648
Iskineport. I’m nervous.

661
00:35:19,673 --> 00:35:22,443
Miss Eva, don’t forget,
he’s the one who brought it!

662
00:35:22,467 --> 00:35:25,236
It’s like he’s giving
you… old people stuff.

663
00:35:25,261 --> 00:35:26,447
Oh, forget it!

664
00:35:26,472 --> 00:35:29,520
- Why?
- You don’t need this!

665
00:35:29,545 --> 00:35:32,441
- What happened to my gift?
- Old people stuff!

666
00:35:32,804 --> 00:35:33,852
I threw it— I threw it away!

667
00:35:38,406 --> 00:35:40,388
Iskineport, who’s old?

668
00:35:41,208 --> 00:35:42,245
Edu.

669
00:35:42,270 --> 00:35:44,271
Oh, okay. Thanks, huh?

670
00:35:44,296 --> 00:35:45,607
Hey, no way!

671
00:35:45,632 --> 00:35:47,547
Barangay Singko,
thank you so much!

672
00:35:47,572 --> 00:35:49,234
Ate Vi, let’s go all out!

673
00:35:49,259 --> 00:35:50,377
- Huh?
- Yeah, let’s go all out!

674
00:35:50,402 --> 00:35:52,561
- Uninvited!
- Uninvited!

675
00:35:54,621 --> 00:35:56,463
- Sorry!
- It’s okay!

676
00:35:56,488 --> 00:36:01,924
I got slapped by Vilma Santos! I made it!
Vilma Santos slapped me! Thank you, Lord!

677
00:36:03,688 --> 00:36:04,803
Uninvited! Uninvited!

678
00:36:06,302 --> 00:36:07,830
We thank you very much for Uninvited.

679
00:36:07,855 --> 00:36:11,713
And thank you also.
And thank you so much to everyone

680
00:36:11,744 --> 00:36:16,502
here at Da Pers Family!
Thank you so much.

681
00:36:25,340 --> 00:36:27,946
Kuya is so in love!

682
00:36:27,971 --> 00:36:29,365
I’m not even sure if we’re official yet.

683
00:36:29,390 --> 00:36:30,460
Have you held hands?

684
00:36:30,494 --> 00:36:31,633
Have you gone on a date?

685
00:36:31,704 --> 00:36:32,632
Have you kissed?

686
00:36:32,657 --> 00:36:33,274
No, what?!

687
00:36:33,299 --> 00:36:34,535
Then what are you?!

688
00:36:34,668 --> 00:36:36,965
Assuming! That’s what you are!

689
00:36:36,990 --> 00:36:38,580
I can’t take this, guys! I’m going home!

690
00:36:38,605 --> 00:36:40,847
Maybe I really am just assuming.

691
00:36:41,534 --> 00:36:43,037
BFF, this is all yours.

692
00:36:43,431 --> 00:36:43,904
Huh?

693
00:36:43,929 --> 00:36:45,186
Is that really Tso K?

694
00:36:45,211 --> 00:36:48,381
Why does he seem so nice? Isn’t
he supposed to be super mean?

695
00:36:48,415 --> 00:36:50,482
- He’s about to kick the bucket!
- Huh?!

696
00:36:50,575 --> 00:36:52,278
All my patients are like that!

697
00:36:52,303 --> 00:36:55,913
When they know their time
is up, they suddenly turn nice!

698
00:36:56,045 --> 00:36:58,596
My BFF is terminally ill?!

699
00:36:59,030 --> 00:37:01,575
I’m an expert when it comes to the ladies!

700
00:37:01,600 --> 00:37:03,789
Hold here, then look into her eyes.

701
00:37:03,814 --> 00:37:05,507
Wow, that’s intense!

702
00:37:05,532 --> 00:37:08,879
Then you lean in… and kiss her.
